# ComposeBus PCB Landscape — Four Real Boards In HAL Terms [SPEC:PCB-BOARDS-OVERVIEW]

> Four real boards, all built to hang off the ComposeBus, and the thing worth reading is not the boards — it is
> what they BREAK. Two are minimal-MCU native peers with an on-board brain (button matrix and CAN gateway, both
> CH32V003); two are ESP32-C3 SuperMini carriers (lego_dots, rack_triple_gauge). Each maps, mostly, onto the nine
> interface kinds of [SPEC:CXC-HAL-DECLARE]. Together they surface five gaps the closed set does not model, and two
> of them break real coverage TODAY: **CAN is a transport/membrane, not a peripheral kind** ([PCB-STRESS-S1], the
> single biggest break), and the **MCP23017 is a pin MULTIPLIER, not a sensor** ([PCB-STRESS-S2]) — on three of the
> four boards, so half the fleet's I/O is unexpressible. Two more were derived INDEPENDENTLY from the opposite
> direction weeks later and agree: S1 anticipated the mothercard/daughtercard CAN-trunk architecture by four weeks,
> and S3's `gauge = {needle + backlight}` is the same conclusion as the widget side's named output channels. A prior
> derivation arriving at the same answer from other evidence is corroboration, and it is why these five are a design
> backlog rather than a wishlist. Source of truth for the hardware is each board's `generate_pcb.py` — there are no
> schematics — cross-checked against KiCad footprint/net extraction and the engineering logs.

- what-this-is: the boards-side companion to the Grove peripheral cross-section. Where the cross-section enumerates the peripheral CATALOG the nine kinds must cover, these four boards are the HOST/CARRIER hardware those peripherals — and the boards themselves — hang off. They are the physical ground truth spec 32 was validated against.
- headline: the boards VALIDATE the nine kinds for leaf peripherals and prove the model is missing four axes: a **transport/membrane** axis (CAN, inter-MCU UART), a **pin-expander role** (MCP23017, on 3 of 4 boards), a **compound-peripheral grouping** (the illuminated matrix, the gauge cluster), and a **stepper/position actuator kind** (L293D + x27.168). [PCB-STRESS-S1] and [PCB-STRESS-S2] BREAK real coverage today; [PCB-STRESS-S3] and [PCB-STRESS-S4] are expressiveness gaps; [PCB-STRESS-S5] is cosmetic.
- topology-finding: **none of the four is a dumb daughtercard.** Every board has a real on-board or socketed MCU able to run ComposeIO firmware — CH32V003 x2, ESP32-C3 x2 — so the native-peer `on:` model of [CXC-HALD-MCU] fits all four at the TOP level and every stress is one level DOWN (expanders, compounds, CAN, steppers). The Software-Defined-Hardware topology the mothercard workstream is designing is already the fleet's actual shape; workstream J is about making it deliberate and self-describing rather than per-board.
- draft-status: DRAFT. Characterisation is David's, 2026-07-18. This derivation is 2026-08-13 and is UNRATIFIED on two points named in the footer: the `PCB-` prefix registration and the `GROUNDS`/`STRESSES` verb registrations. Deliberately NOT a `status` key: the value is prose, and a prose `status` reads to the linter as a lifecycle claim it cannot honour.
- depends-on: [SPEC:CXC-HAL-DECLARE]
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-BOARD-HW], [SPEC:CXC-VISION], [PCB-INDEX], [PCB-HAL-STRESS], [PCB-CORPUS-PLACEMENT], [PCB-PROVENANCE], [PCB-GAUGE3-GPIO5-CONFLICT]

