## 1. How these facts are known, and why they are here

### [PCB-PROVENANCE] Three independent sources, and not one schematic among them

- definition: how every identity in this document is known. It matters more than usual here, because the normal instrument does not exist: these boards have no schematic to read.
- no-schematic: none of the four has a `.kicad_sch`. Each is emitted DIRECTLY to `.kicad_pcb` by a per-board `generate_pcb.py` — a net table plus placed footprints, then Freerouting. So every KiCad tool that defers to the schematic (`extract_i2c_devices`, `list_schematic_components`, `analyze_pcb_nets`) returns nothing usable on this tree, and an analyst who reaches for them concludes the boards are empty.
- three-sources: identities are triangulated from (1) `list_pcb_footprints` plus net names grepped out of the `.kicad_pcb` S-expression text, (2) each board's `generate_pcb.py` docstring and net map, and (3) the per-board `logs/engineering/*.jsonl`. Three independent sources agreeing is exactly what the HIGH confidence below means — not one tool's opinion.
- what-is-inferred: the ComposeBus ATTACH INTENT and the semantic-namespace names. Neither is in any file; both are read off David's framing. Every board node carries them under `inferred` so they never read as extracted fact.
- confidence: 0.9
- confidence-derivation: 0.9 encodes David's word HIGH for parts and topology. **The numeral is this derivation's, not David's** — he wrote an enum value and SPEC 7.1 requires a float, so the mapping is an authoring choice and is flagged for ratify. Attach-intent is materially lower and is deliberately NOT folded into this number, because one averaged figure would flatter the weakest claim in the document.
- part-of: [SPEC:PCB-BOARDS-OVERVIEW]

### [PCB-CORPUS-PLACEMENT] Why this is a derivation in the corpus and `pcb/` is NOT a registered corpus root

- decision: the PCB landscape enters the queryable corpus as THIS derivation, now living under its own registered corpus directory `corpora/pcb-specs/` (moved 2026-09-02 from `corpora/platform-specs/` per David's ruling — a separate corpus, not a subdirectory of platform-specs). (a local path, not published) is still deliberately NOT registered as a corpus root; that question is orthogonal to which git-tracked directory this derivation itself lives in. The two options below were weighed and they are mutually exclusive, which is what forced that original choice.
- placement-update-2026-09-02: moved from `corpora/platform-specs/64-pcb-board-landscape.lts` to `corpora/pcb-specs/64-pcb-board-landscape.lts` and registered as its own `pcb-specs` corpus in `FACTLATTICE_CORPUS_CONFIG`, plus added as an additional `specs` root on the multi-root corpora that already cited `PCB-*` ids out of platform-specs (intelligence-console, visual-composer, headless-monitor), so the existing citations in specs 32/62/69/71 and the decision graph keep resolving. This does NOT reopen `not-registered-unversioned`/`mutually-exclusive` below — those govern the ungitted (a local path, not published) raw source, which is still not registered and still not mirrored.
- not-registered-unversioned: (a local path, not published) is **not a git repository** — measured 2026-08-13, `git rev-parse` fails at that path and at every parent. Registering it would make in-repo specs depend on a tree with no history, no diff and no review gate.
- not-registered-machine-local: the corpus registry is `~/factlattice-internal-dev/private/corpus-config.json` — GITIGNORED and machine-local (renamed from `~/factlattice-deployment/` since this was first written; corrected 2026-09-02). A registration there is invisible in any diff, unreviewable by the architect, absent on any other machine and absent at open-source release. The citations it would satisfy live in `corpora/platform-specs/32-*.lts` and `62-*.lts`, which are in-repo and travel. A machine-local fix leaves those citations dangling everywhere except one laptop.
- not-registered-lossy-source: the source document is **already silently lossy**, measured against the live parser 2026-08-13: 46 authored `- ` bullets, **27 parsed properties**. All five stresses mint NOTHING (each line opens `- **(S1) ...`, a markdown-emphasis key region), and `mcu / brains`, `connectors / ports`, `peripherals / I/O` mint nothing on EVERY board node (spaces and slashes in the key region), as do `non-stresses worth recording` and `headline for the architect`. `[PCB-HAL-STRESS]` parsed to exactly two properties: `definition` and `part-of`. Registering that file would register a document whose load-bearing content is invisible to query. The fold-in had to be a RE-AUTHORING wherever it landed.
- mutually-exclusive: this derivation reuses the SAME `PCB-*` ids, which is what makes the existing citations in specs 32 and 62 resolve. If `pcb/` were also registered into the same corpus, every one of those ids would be defined TWICE — a collision in which the first definition wins and every traversal to the loser is silently wrong. So registration is not merely redundant now, it is excluded.
- authority-split: hardware ground truth stays in (a local path, not published): the `.kicad_pcb` files, the per-board `generate_pcb.py`, and `logs/engineering/*.jsonl` are the actual sources and are NOT mirrored here. This document is authoritative only for the HAL characterisation and the stress synthesis — which is architecture, not hardware, and whose consumers (specs 32, 60, 62 and the fleet plan) are all in-repo.
- sync-contract: `derived-from` in the frontmatter names the source path AND its sha256 at extraction. Drift is therefore DETECTABLE by one command rather than by hope: `shasum -a 256 (a local path, not published)` — if it differs from the recorded digest, the source moved and this derivation is stale. That is the property `60-board-hardware-inventory.lts.bak` did not have.
- resync-trigger: re-derive when (a) the digest changes, (b) a board is revised in KiCad, or (c) a fifth board is added to (a local path, not published). The re-derivation is a re-read of the three sources at [PCB-PROVENANCE], not a diff of two prose files.
- residual-risk-stated: the trigger is a CONVENTION, not an enforced check — nothing runs `shasum` on a schedule today. An edit to the source will not announce itself; it will only be catchable. That is a real weakening versus registration and it is recorded rather than glossed.
- part-of: [SPEC:PCB-BOARDS-OVERVIEW]

